[[31,63,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The rear fog lamps activation signal reaches pin 35 of connector\n              B of \n                              \n                              <strong>M1</strong>\n                              \n                                from the control button in the panel.</p><p>The side lights activation signal is sent\n              to pin 28 of connector B of the Body Computer \n                              \n                              <strong>M1</strong>\n                              \n                                from the\n              steering column switch unit \n                              \n                              <strong>H5</strong><a href=\"#/3023183\">E2010</a>\n                              \n                               ].</p><p>The dipped headlamps activation signal is\n              sent to pin 4 of connector D of the Body Computer \n                              \n                              <strong>M1</strong>\n                              \n                                from\n              the steering colun switch unit \n                              \n                              <strong>H5</strong>\n                              \n                               El2011].</p><p>The fog lights activation signal reaches\n              pin 1 of connector D of the Body Computer \n                              \n                              <strong>M1</strong>\n                              \n                                (see EL2030].</p><p>The &#x27;ignition ON&#x27; signal (INT) for the switch \n              \n                              \n                              <strong>H1</strong>\n                              \n                                reaches the underdashboard control unit \n                              \n                              <strong>B2</strong>\n                              \n                                at\n              pin 11 of connector H and from there moves on to the Body Computer \n                              \n                              <strong>M1</strong>\n                              \n                               \n              (pin 9 of connector F).</p><p>The Body Computer \n                              \n                              <strong>M1</strong>\n                              \n                               controls the\n              supply of the rear fog lamp \n                              \n                              <strong>F35</strong>\n                              \n                                from pin 31 of connector\n              E.</p><p>The signal is sent, from pin 21 of connector\n              C of \n                              \n                              <strong>M1</strong>\n                              \n                               , to light up the LED in the control button \n                              \n                              <strong>H12</strong>\n                              \n                               .</p><p>The Body Computer \n                              \n                              <strong>M1</strong>\n                              \n                                is connected,\n              via the CAN line, to the instrument panel \n                              \n                              <strong>E50</strong>\n                              \n                                to manage\n              the &#x27;lights failure&#x27; warning light if there is a failure in the\n              circuit.</p>"]]